   "source": [
    "### 1. Analytical Solution of Linear System\n",
    "For $\\frac{d\\mathbf{y}}{dt} = \\begin{bmatrix} -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 \\end{bmatrix} \\mathbf{y}$ with $\\mathbf{y}(0) = [2, -3]^T$:\n",
    "- $y_1(t) = 2 e^{-t}$\n",
    "- $y_2(t) = -3 e^{-2t}$"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "from scipy.integrate import solve_ivp\n",
    "\n",
    "def sys_ode(t, y):\n",
    "    return [-y[0], -2*y[1]]\n",
    "\n",
    "sol = solve_ivp(sys_ode, (0, 2), [2, -3], t_eval=[2.0])\n",
    "print(\"Numerical Solution at t=2:\", sol.y[:, 0])\n",
    "print(\"Analytical Solution at t=2:\", [2*np.exp(-2.0), -3*np.exp(-4.0)])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 2. Implement Euler's Method from Scratch"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def euler_ode(h):\n",
    "    t_vals = np.arange(0, 2+h, h)\n",
    "    y = 1.0\n",
    "    for _ in t_vals[:-1]:\n",
    "        y = y + h * y\n",
    "    return y\n",
    "\n",
    "y_01 = euler_ode(0.1)\n",
    "y_001 = euler_ode(0.01)\n",
    "true_val = np.exp(2.0)\n",
    "print(f\"True: {true_val:.4f}, h=0.1: {y_01:.4f} (Err: {abs(y_01-true_val):.4f}), h=0.01: {y_001:.4f} (Err: {abs(y_001-true_val):.4f})\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 3. Linearization and Equilibrium\n",
    "For $f(x, y) = y - 1 = 0 \\implies y^* = 1$.\n",
    "For $g(x, y) = x^2 - y = 0 \\implies x^2 - 1 = 0 \\implies x^* = \\pm 1$.\n",
    "Equilibrium points: $(1, 1)$ and $(-1, 1)$.\n",
    "\n",
    "Jacobian: $J(x, y) = \\begin{bmatrix} 0 & 1 \\\\ 2x & -1 \\end{bmatrix}$.\n",
    "- At $(1, 1)$: $J = \\begin{bmatrix} 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 \\end{bmatrix}$. Eigenvalues: $\\det(J-\\lambda I) = \\lambda^2 + \\lambda - 2 = (\\lambda+2)(\\lambda-1) = 0 \\implies \\lambda = 1, -2$. Bounded positive real part: **Saddle/Unstable**.\n",
    "- At $(-1, 1)$: $J = \\begin{bmatrix} 0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -1 \\end{bmatrix}$. Eigenvalues: $\\lambda^2 + \\lambda + 2 = 0 \\implies \\lambda = \\frac{-1 \\pm i\\sqrt{7}}{2}$. Negative real part: **Stable Spiral**."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Stability verified analytically."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 4. RK4 Implementation"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def f_pendulum(t, state):\n",
    "    theta, omega = state\n",
    "    return [omega, -np.sin(theta)]\n",
    "\n",
    "def rk4_step(f, t, y, h):\n",
    "    k1 = np.array(f(t, y))\n",
    "    k2 = np.array(f(t + h/2, y + h*k1/2))\n",
    "    k3 = np.array(f(t + h/2, y + h*k2/2))\n",
    "    k4 = np.array(f(t + h, y + h*k3))\n",
    "    return y + (h/6.0) * (k1 + 2*k2 + 2*k3 + k4)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Simulate pendulum trajectory\n",
    "h = 0.05\n",
    "t_eval = np.arange(0, 10, h)\n",
    "state = np.array([2.0, 0.0])  # release from 2 radians\n",
    "path = [state.copy()]\n",
    "\n",
    "for t in t_eval[:-1]:\n",
    "    state = rk4_step(f_pendulum, t, state, h)\n",
    "    path.append(state.copy())\n",
    "path = np.array(path)\n",
    "print(\"RK4 Simulation final state (theta, omega):\", path[-1])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
